---
import Card from '../components/ui/Card.astro';
import Container from '../components/ui/Container.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/ui/PageIntro.astro';
import { resolveSiteHref } from '../lib/paths';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Packages" description="Choose the Forge initializer, content models, browser formatter, and frontmatter lint rule.">
  <Container class="space-y-10 pb-16">
    <PageIntro eyebrow="Packages" title="Four packages. One owned site.">
      <p>Use the initializer once to create a site. Adopt the libraries and lint rule independently as your project needs them. Each package has its own version and compatibility contract; their versions do not move in lockstep.</p>
    </PageIntro>
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <Card size="lg"><div class="badge badge-neutral font-mono">Initializer</div><h2 class="card-title text-2xl"><code class="wrap-anywhere">@rm-industries/create-forge</code></h2><p>Validates project inputs, safely materializes the tested template snapshot, installs dependencies, and optionally initializes Git.</p><div class="card-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@rm-industries/create-forge">View on npm</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href={resolveSiteHref('/docs/create-forge/')}>Reference</a></div></Card>
      <Card size="lg"><div class="badge badge-neutral font-mono">Library</div><h2 class="card-title text-2xl"><code class="wrap-anywhere">@rm-industries/content-model</code></h2><p>Provides integration-neutral content definitions with matching Astro and Sveltia adapters. It can evolve independently after generation.</p><div class="card-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@rm-industries/content-model">View on npm</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href={resolveSiteHref('/docs/content-model/')}>Reference</a></div></Card>
      <Card size="lg"><div class="badge badge-neutral font-mono">Browser formatter</div><h2 class="card-title text-2xl"><code class="wrap-anywhere">@rm-industries/browser-oxfmt</code></h2><p>Formats Markdown locally in a worker with the native Oxfmt engine compiled to WebAssembly. A Node build helper aligns browser options with your repository policy.</p><div class="card-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@rm-industries/browser-oxfmt">View on npm</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href={resolveSiteHref('/docs/browser-oxfmt/')}>Reference</a></div></Card>
      <Card size="lg"><div class="badge badge-neutral font-mono">Lint rule</div><h2 class="card-title text-2xl"><code class="wrap-anywhere">@rm-industries/markdownlint-frontmatter</code></h2><p>Checks and fixes YAML frontmatter key order through Markdownlint. It preserves values and body text, and can derive field order from a content model without depending on Astro or a CMS.</p><div class="card-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@rm-industries/markdownlint-frontmatter">View on npm</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href={resolveSiteHref('/docs/markdownlint-frontmatter/')}>Reference</a></div></Card>
    </div>
    <p>The create-forge reference describes the intended 2.0 contract. Check npm availability before selecting that version; updating an initializer does not upgrade generated application source.</p>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>
